WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.950
<b>Episode 15     A Small Step</b>

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.080
Hey, did you buy some yet?

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.380
They're just obligatory chocolates, though.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.770
It's almost Valentine's Day again—

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.510
What happened last year?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.550
Didn't you give anything to Ken-chan?

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.890
She bought some, but never handed them to him.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.220
In the end, she ate them herself.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.480
Mitsue-chan!

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.520
How about giving him some this year?

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.520
You've gotten a lot closer with him.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.860
You have a pretty good chance.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.440
You think?

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.780
Will he accept them?

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.200
Ken-chan will be happy to eat them!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.570
Even if he doesn't understand 
the intentions behind them.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.790
Are there still boys around that 
don't know about Valentine's Day?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.620
I tell him every year, but then he forgets it again.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.920
Ken-chan doesn't waste brain cells 
on things he's not interested in.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.340
In that case, simply handing them over isn't enough.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.590
You have to confess to him at the same time.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.130
Ah, Ken-chan.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.220
What's up?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.220
My imagination won't flare up.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.810
Tell the teacher I'll be late for fifth period.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.900
Ken-chan, do you know what kind 
of day the 14th of February is?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.560
I do.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.860
Note: February 14th, when written as 2/14 - 2 is read as "ni", 1 as "bo", 4 as "shi" - niboshi are dried sardines.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.860
It's the day of dried sardines.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.510
Dried sardines, huh?

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.070
Those are nice too—

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.410
Dried sardines— is he serious?

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.410
Probably.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.330
Ken-chan loves them.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.120
Your rivals are dried sardines—

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.270
I see, it's that season again—

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.980
May my wish reach the gods

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.980
Love 
fulfillment

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.980
That's why we're seeing so 
many wishes of the romantic kind.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.860
Yashima-sama, do you like chocolates?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.070
Yes, I love them!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.870
When lightly broiled, they go great together with miso!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.540
Chocolate does?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.410
Yes.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.430
I'm telling you, you have to heat it up in hot water first.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.010
I see.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.640
Can't you just kamichu something up in a flash?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.230
Stop it, Yurie finally got in the mood to do this!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.400
You have to give them as a 
middle school girl, not as a god.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.320
That's right.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.150
Down with those sardines!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.330
Welcome home!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.160
I hear you're making chocolates?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.830
Thanks for having us.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.000
Thanks.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.080
I thought these might come in handy.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.590
Use as much of them as you want.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.670
Chocolates, huh.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.510
You're finally at the age to do 
girly things like that, huh, Matsuri.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.720
Yurie's the one making them.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.850
I'm just a spectator.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.020
Oh really?

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.690
Don't you have anyone you want to give chocolates to?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.530
No one.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.780
I see—

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.450
Spring is still so far away—

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.500
We'll be third year students next year.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.510
Almost time to start studying for exams.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.810
When we become high school students,

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.850
we'll be going to school again.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.810
Are we going to leave this town someday after that?

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.330
You're the heir to this shrine, so you'll 
have to come back eventually, won't you?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.790
Guess so.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.710
But I don't know yet.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.710
In any case, I'll have to start making some plans.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.260
Miko has her capabilities—

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.640
And I might find my calling along the line.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.240
And you, Mitsue-chan?

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.140
What do you want to become in the future?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.560
I thought I'd become a housewife—

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.270
Of that cousin of yours?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.940
How would I know!?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.400
I still haven't decided on becoming 
a housewife or something else—

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.240
I can't even estimate what 
will happen to me from now on.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.410
What about you?

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.410
What do you want to become?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.710
You're more than welcome 
to become our permanent god.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.750
I don't know yet either.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.930
I don't know, but in order to decide that—

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.980
I'd like to have some courage.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.450
I see.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.200
So you made chocolates.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.790
You're in the middle of your youth, of course.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.910
Truly.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.420
So, who will you give them to?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.340
Secret.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:28.880
But I made enough for dad 
and Shou-chan, so don't worry.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.220
I'm glad to have been born to become a father.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.680
I don't want them, I don't like sweet things.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.770
I went to the trouble of making them, so eat them!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.310
Don't you have any chocolate for me?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.000
Nope.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.900
You're my mother, after all.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.770
How mean.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.610
Are you trying to fence me off from you and the boys?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.950
No need to cry, Akane-san.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.700
On White Day,

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.990
I'll give you enough candy to 
fill Kourakuen Stadium four times!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.290
How wonderful!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.830
But that'll give me cavities—

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.760
That's the end.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.350
Hello, Hitotsubashi household.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.940
Oh, Yurie?

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.320
Mitsue-chan! What's up?

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.610
I have something to do tomorrow 
morning, so I'm going ahead.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.220
Something to do?

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.990
Did you have cleaning duty?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.910
Yeah, something like that.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:38.990
See you tomorrow.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.670
What's wrong?

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:49.920
It's nothing!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.260
Yurie-sama!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:53.510
It's Team Happiness!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.930
I like you, I like you, I love you!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.390
Say "I love you," and I will love you back!

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.770
Say "Je t'aime," and we will be in love forever!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:06.980
These days only romantic requests 
come in, and since they're all alike,

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.110
we decided to let you pick one by yourself.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:14.030
"I'm having harsh romantic troubles. 
Please give me some advice."

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.570
This one came from the Prime Minister.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.500
But the Prime Minister is married.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.460
<i>Love to humans is like catnip to cats.</i>

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.340
<i>Once you fall in love, your situation 
or age don't matter anymore.</i>

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.630
<i>Anyway, he has little use for your advice.</i>

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:41.310
With your powers, even if you're facing 
a grown man, everything will work out.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.390
"A drowning man will grasp at even a straw."

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.430
Anyway, since the majority has to do with Valentine's Day,

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.240
Are you saying Yurie-sama is a straw!?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.180
they'll be settled by tomorrow one way or another.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.310
That's right.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.820
I can't fix people's romances using my kamichu powers.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.240
I hope things work out for you tomorrow as well.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.030
Yeah—

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:06.460
He's such a lucky person to be able to 
receive chocolates from you, Yurie-sama.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.170
You think?

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.750
I made enough for all of you, 
so I'll give you some tomorrow.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.800
Do we get chocolates too!?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.970
Really?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.430
All right!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.680
Chocolates! Chocolates! Chocolates!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.770
I have some for you as well.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.190
Thank you very much!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.600
I'm so happy!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.440
I have some for you too, Bin-chan.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.990
Really?

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:41.090
That's the first time in my life!

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.530
<i>Don't I get anything?</i>

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:48.370
Well, you're Tama.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.560
Good morning!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.560
Good morning.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.820
Yurie-chan, fight!

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.120
Do your best!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.240
Fear is greater than the danger!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.020
Will it work out?

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.590
Don't worry, it's perfect!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.600
Good morning.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.350
Good morning.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:49.980
Good morning.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.310
Did you bring the chocolates?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.780
Yep.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.650
Still no good?

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.780
The big one just won't come out.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.210
It looks like I forgot them—

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.630
I wanted to bring them in a bag 
because the ribbon kept falling off.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.340
But with my sleepyhead this morning,

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.760
I completely forgot about that—

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.810
Ken-chan said he had to work again after class.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.400
In the neighboring town this time.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:39.070
Lunch break is your only 
chance to give it to him today.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.650
What should I do?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.740
Leave it to us.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.280
I'll go get the chocolates at 
your house during lunch break.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.750
But I was the one who forgot to bring them—

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.420
At your pace, you'll never make it.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:13:00.590
All of us will prevent Ken-chan from going anywhere.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:02.920
All of us?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:13.230
"I cannot help being less handsome than Jim."

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:17.690
"Cannot," followed by "help," means "it can't be helped".

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.900
"I was born ugly."

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:19.900
Sign: Operation Yurie - Strategy Plan

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.530
"What have I done wrong?"

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:22.610
That's what it's about.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.570
Listen well, you guys especially.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.780
Who cares about Jim, it's the inside that counts!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.950
Hitotsubashi Yurie-san is 
pretty cute in her own way, huh?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.120
She gave it her all to help me with my problems,

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.290
and Hitotsubashi Yurie-san is pretty 
popular amongst the boys as well!

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.090
Was there an aureole here?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:43.820
Dunno.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.760
It must be due to the grace of Hitotsubashi 
Yurie-san, who gave us consult yesterday!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:50.600
Really. It's all thanks to Hitotsubashi Yurie!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.810
Ninomiya-kun, are you using 
the roof during lunch again today?

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:05.280
The student council is saying they 
want you to file a request to use it.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.450
But I didn't have to until now—

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.260
It's from today on!

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:12.870
Are you using the roof?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:13.870
Yup.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.000
To Matsuri-chan:
On the roof during lunch

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.090
If the value of x increases, the value of y decreases.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.800
However, it will never reach 0.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.130
Operation Yurie

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.850
Eat this on the ferry.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.190
Well, I'm going.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.530
Mitsue-chan, I'm sorry.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.550
It's all right.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.280
You should start thinking up your confession lines.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.320
Be careful!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.530
Be back soon!

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.370
Do your best!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.500
Be careful!

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.380
Everyone, keep watch over Ken-chan,

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.050
and subtly gossip about Yurie while doing so.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:12.220
Why are you all doing this for me?

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.600
I'm sure you have people to give chocolates to as well—

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.520
You've been giving us advice 
on many things up until now.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.570
It's good to return something to the 
gods every now and then, isn't it?

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.740
My, you too?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.700
Yes.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.200
Shall we go together?

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.250
Hitotsubashi-kun.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:51.930
Here.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.720
To thank you for the trouble I've caused you.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:03.730
Thanks.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.690
It might taste a little strange—

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:07.980
That's okay.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.690
I like chocolate.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.110
To Yashima-sama

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.110
Miko

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.960
Thanks a lot.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.720
Don't mention it.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.010
I'm bringing this to her now!

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:35.260
Tell her to do her best!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.180
I will!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.520
Don't fall out!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.830
Ninomiya-kun is by himself.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.950
He seems to be in deep thought.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:01.870
Thanks.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:06.960
If someone tries to go onto the roof, 
stop them and explain the situation.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:07.830
Got it!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.680
How are you doing? Are you ready for it?

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.730
I'm getting more and more nervous.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.900
Now that it's become such a big thing—

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:32.070
What should I do if he refuses?

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.070
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.360
Nothing I can do about it?

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:40.870
I'll never be able to talk to him again!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.910
Then are you fine with the way things are?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.870
Everyone faces that same dilemma.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.040
Not me, though.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.630
At times like those, people feel like asking god for help!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.780
Please make Yurie-chan happy.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.740
Everybody is helping you right now

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.360
because they know what you're going through.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.790
Please!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.030
Okay!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.200
They're the same as you.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.490
Hurry up, don't falter!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.340
But, you have to muster up the 
last bit of courage by yourself!

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.380
Isn't that right?

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:35.130
Matsuri-chan, amazing—

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:37.550
That's right.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.090
Shrine maidens are amazing.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.760
Yurie-sama!

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:43.100
It's a cat!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.720
Bin-chan!

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.100
Where's Mitsue-chan?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.640
She's right behind me.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.390
Take this.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.950
<i>Do your best, Yurie-chan.</i>

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.050
Stay cool.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.090
Do your best!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.010
Relax!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:18.960
Fight!

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:19.880
It's all right.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.220
Go for it!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.050
How cute!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:24.050
It talked!

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:24.640
Why?

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.260
Because it's a god's cat?

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.520
Do your best!

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.430
Fight!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.490
Mitsue-chan!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:45.410
Go for it!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:47.840
I will!

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:57.920
Good luck!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.160
Ninomiya-kun—

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:34.920
Ninomiya-kun.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.670
Hitotsubashi-san?

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.380
Sorry, not right now—

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.970
Ninomiya-kun!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.520
What's up?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:06.870
How are things?

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.370
It's about to start.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.540
Hitotsubashi-san?

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.510
Ninomiya-kun.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:35.770
I— have always liked you.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:44.860
I love you.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:49.200
If it's all right with you, please go out with me!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.880
I see—

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:07.550
That's what it was!

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:11.510
That was it!

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.720
Why did I never notice?

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:17.440
Umm—

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:19.270
Sorry, hold on for a second!

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.100
Yurie-chan, can you read it?

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:57.770
Y-Yes!

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.340
Sign: Love

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:17.660
I figured it out just now.

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:24.630
I liked you as well.

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:55.030
Er— this is— umm—

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:14.550
What the—

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:20.180
Yurie-sama!

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:22.730
Congratulations!

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:23.650
It's a miracle.

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:25.610
Everyone—

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:27.610
Amazing!

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:30.280
I'm flying again!

00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:40.250
What a strong wind—

00:24:40.250 --> 00:24:41.450
They're flying!

00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:42.000
That's a god for you.

00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:47.750
The day that a strong wind blows, if 
you confess your love on the roof—

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:50.460
This'll be a hit!

00:24:51.630 --> 00:24:52.920
Thank goodness.

00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:56.430
<i>Do your best, Yurie-chan!</i>

00:24:58.140 --> 00:25:00.060
Finally, something interesting happens!

00:25:03.890 --> 00:25:06.310
Is that Yurie-chan?

00:25:07.270 --> 00:25:08.820
You think it went well?

00:25:09.190 --> 00:25:10.330
I'm sure of it!

00:25:10.330 --> 00:25:12.490
They're soaring so high through the sky!

00:25:15.740 --> 00:25:18.160
They're in high spirits, aren't they bro?

00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:19.830
I'll forgive them.

00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:21.750
Ah, young ones—

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:23.260
Congratulations!

00:25:23.260 --> 00:25:24.710
I'm happy for you!

00:25:31.710 --> 00:25:37.640
I guess you could say only god knows 
what will happen to Yurie-sama from now.

00:25:46.980 --> 00:25:50.060
Kenji-kun, what you said just now—

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.860
Is it true that you like me?

00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:55.740
Yes, I love you.

00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:01.160
Because you're strange.

00:26:03.450 --> 00:26:04.330
Strange?

00:26:05.210 --> 00:26:07.170
It'll be stimulating if we're together.

00:26:07.170 --> 00:26:08.290
Because you're strange.

00:26:09.830 --> 00:26:10.670
Strange?

00:26:10.670 --> 00:26:12.960
Because I'm not strange at all.

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:14.050
It'll be fun!

00:26:14.880 --> 00:26:16.590
Let's have a great time together!

00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:23.560
Yeah!

00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:25.350
Sign: Love

00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:27.060
Sign: Strange

00:26:47.330 --> 00:26:53.390
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:26:47.330 --> 00:26:53.390
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:26:53.390 --> 00:26:58.300
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:26:53.390 --> 00:26:58.300
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:26:59.310 --> 00:27:05.350
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:26:59.310 --> 00:27:05.350
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:27:05.350 --> 00:27:10.470
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:27:05.350 --> 00:27:10.470
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:27:11.390 --> 00:27:14.410
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:27:11.390 --> 00:27:14.410
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:27:14.410 --> 00:27:17.380
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:27:14.410 --> 00:27:17.380
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:20.380
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:20.380
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:22.970
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:22.970
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:30.610
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:30.610
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:27:30.610 --> 00:27:36.650
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:27:30.610 --> 00:27:36.650
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:27:36.650 --> 00:27:42.140
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:27:36.650 --> 00:27:42.140
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:27:42.440 --> 00:27:49.560
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:27:42.440 --> 00:27:49.560
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:27:53.790 --> 00:28:16.790
<b>Preview</b>

00:27:54.860 --> 00:27:56.770
It's the warm and carefree spring vacation!

00:27:57.280 --> 00:28:01.070
Before becoming third year students, it's 
time to cleanse the mind and the shrine!

00:28:01.490 --> 00:28:04.570
Spring will be a little bit different this year.

00:28:04.570 --> 00:28:07.620
Because I'm with Kenji-kun this year!

00:28:08.620 --> 00:28:11.040
Next time, "Look, Spring Has Come".

00:28:09.540 --> 00:28:16.790
<b>Look, Spring Has Come</b>

00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:13.000
For the last time, all together:

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.080
Chuchuu!
